==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|einn|lang=non}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|ainaz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{recons|óynos|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Faroese and Norwegian Nynorsk {{term|ein|lang=fo}}, Danish and Norwegian Bokmål {{term|en|lang=da}}.

===Numeral===
'''einn''' {{m}}, '''[[ein]]''' {{f}}, '''[[eitt]]''' {{n}}

# '''[[one]]'''; the cardinal number after [[núll#Icelandic|núll]] and before [[tveir#Icelandic|tveir]].
# {{accusative}} masculine {{singular}} form of [[einn#Icelandic|einn]]

